< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/101#issuecomment-6800694239 Blocked-by: #113
The fix for #101 is ready and queued to land again, but it hasn't merged yet. #101 stays open and is now marked `Blocked-by: #113`.

- **Why the last land failed:** the gates didn't fail. The build job (pipeline 3054366892) never reported, and the manager gave up with "no verdict within 3h". That is the stall in #113, where triggered builds never start; #113 is itself waiting on tacplus-dev/cluster#18. #127's build stalled the same way today.
- **What's queued:** commit 2fc8da8, queued with the manager at 16:01Z on main 5301129. It is the same change the previous run tried to land as 0b2cde7.
  - Trivy and OSV-Scanner are now built the way gitleaks and Syft already are, requiring `github.com/klauspost/compress` v1.20.2.
  - gitleaks also requires compress v1.20.2 and `github.com/andybalholm/brotli` v1.2.7; Syft also requires brotli v1.2.7.
  - The image build checks that each fixed version is the one actually built in.
  - The README's security table names each override and when it can be dropped.
  - PROPOSALS.md has a follow-up: run govulncheck on the scanners during the image build.
- **What's verified:** the full gates passed locally on the previous run. An earlier run's image build of this same Dockerfile change passed the scanner checks, and govulncheck found neither advisory. No build job has run on this exact commit, because of #113.

I posted this status as a comment on #101. If this land also comes back red only because the build job never ran, the next run will land it again once #113 is closed.
